      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To quantify neighborhood volatility, you can incorporate indicators like business_license_volume, employed_to_population_ratio, and Amopy's Score (Amusement Areas & Possibilities of crowdier slum areas). Specifically, for business density and turnover, consider the following metrics:\n\n- Number of new businesses per year\n- Average time-to-replacement (i.e., the average tenure of businesses)\n- Industry-specific turnover rates (e.g., high rate of restaurant business closures may indicate a volatile area)\n- Local economic indicators, such as unemployment rates and poverty levels, which may reflect community instability",
      "source": "target",
